---
import ToolLayout from '../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
---
<ToolLayout title="Margin & Markup Calculator" category="Business" description="Set a selling price from your target margin or markup. Or enter a selling price to see your profit, including the effect of a discount.">
 <div class="kit-workspace"><form class="kit-panel" id="margin-form"><div class="kit-row"><h2>1. Enter your numbers</h2><button class="kit-btn" type="button" id="margin-example">Try an example</button></div>
 <div class="kit-field"><label for="margin-mode">Calculate using</label><select id="margin-mode"><option value="margin">Target gross margin (%)</option><option value="markup">Markup on cost (%)</option><option value="price">A selling price I already have</option></select></div>
 <div class="kit-fields"><div class="kit-field"><label for="margin-cost">Unit cost</label><input id="margin-cost" type="number" min="0" max="1000000000" step="0.01" placeholder="75.00" required/></div><div class="kit-field"><label for="margin-currency">Currency</label><select id="margin-currency">{['USD','LKR','QAR','GBP','EUR','INR','AED'].map(c=><option value={c}>{c}</option>)}</select></div></div>
 <div class="kit-field"><label for="margin-value" id="margin-value-label">Target margin (%)</label><input id="margin-value" type="number" min="0" max="99.99" step="0.01" placeholder="25" required/></div>
 <div class="kit-field"><label for="margin-discount">Discount on selling price (%)</label><input id="margin-discount" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.01" value="0" required/><p class="kit-help">The target sets the price before discount. A discount then reduces your achieved margin.</p></div>
 <button class="kit-btn primary" type="submit">Calculate →</button><p class="kit-status kit-error" id="margin-error" role="alert"></p></form>
 <section class="kit-panel kit-result" aria-labelledby="margin-result-title"><h2 id="margin-result-title">2. Your pricing breakdown</h2><div id="margin-empty"><p class="kit-help">Enter your numbers to see the selling price and what you keep after unit cost.</p></div><div id="margin-output" hidden><p class="kit-help">Selling price before discount</p><div class="kit-big-number" id="margin-price"></div><dl><div><dt>After discount</dt><dd id="margin-discounted"></dd></div><div><dt>Unit cost</dt><dd id="margin-unit-cost"></dd></div><div><dt>Gross profit per unit</dt><dd id="margin-profit"></dd></div><div><dt>Achieved gross margin</dt><dd id="margin-percent"></dd></div><div><dt>Achieved markup</dt><dd id="margin-markup"></dd></div></dl><p id="margin-warning" class="kit-help"></p><div class="kit-actions"><button class="kit-btn" id="margin-copy">Copy breakdown</button><a class="kit-btn" href="/tools/quotation-builder/">Build a quotation ↗</a></div></div><p class="kit-status" id="margin-status" role="status"></p><p class="kit-help">Uses your chosen currency as a label; no currency conversion. Excludes taxes, fees and overhead unless included in your cost.</p></section></div>
 <p class="kit-note">✓ Calculations stay in your browser. No account or upload needed.</p>
 <section class="kit-guide" id="guide"><h2>Margin and markup answer different questions.</h2><div class="kit-guide-grid"><div><h3>Gross margin</h3><p>Profit ÷ selling price × 100. If an item costs 75 and sells for 100, profit is 25 and gross margin is 25%.</p></div><div><h3>Markup</h3><p>Profit ÷ cost × 100. For the same item, markup is 25 ÷ 75 × 100, or 33.33%. A 25% markup is not a 25% margin.</p></div><div><h3>A discount changes profit</h3><p>A 10% discount reduces that 100 price to 90. With cost still at 75, profit falls to 15 and achieved margin becomes 16.67%.</p></div></div><details><summary>Which formulas and rounding rules are used?</summary><p>Target-margin price = cost ÷ (1 − margin ÷ 100). Markup price = cost × (1 + markup ÷ 100). Target prices round up to the next cent to meet the target before discount. Discounted prices and profit round to two decimal places. Achieved percentages use those rounded amounts.</p></details><details><summary>Why can’t I enter a 100% target margin?</summary><p>With a positive cost, a 100% margin would require an unbounded selling price. A zero selling price has an undefined margin, and zero cost has an undefined markup; these appear as N/A. Below-cost sales show a negative gross profit.</p></details><details><summary>Is this my final business profit?</summary><p>No. This is a per-unit gross calculation from the cost you provide. Include relevant unit costs, and separately account for overhead, payment fees, tax and other expenses. For further planning, explore the <a href="/prompts/pricing-strategy/">pricing strategy prompt</a>.</p></details></section>
</ToolLayout>
<script>
import {calculateMargin} from '../../../utils/business-tools.mjs';
import {copyText} from '../../../utils/tool-browser';
const get=<T extends HTMLElement>(id:string)=>document.getElementById(id) as T;
const mode=get<HTMLSelectElement>('margin-mode'),cost=get<HTMLInputElement>('margin-cost'),value=get<HTMLInputElement>('margin-value'),discount=get<HTMLInputElement>('margin-discount'),currency=get<HTMLSelectElement>('margin-currency');
let summary='';
function invalidate(){get('margin-output').hidden=true;get('margin-empty').hidden=false;get('margin-error').textContent='';get('margin-status').textContent='';summary='';}
get('margin-form').addEventListener('input',invalidate);
mode.addEventListener('change',()=>{get('margin-value-label').textContent=mode.value==='price'?'Selling price':mode.value==='markup'?'Markup (%)':'Target margin (%)';value.max=mode.value==='margin'?'99.99':mode.value==='markup'?'10000':'1000000000';value.value='';invalidate();});
get('margin-example').addEventListener('click',()=>{mode.value='margin';get('margin-value-label').textContent='Target margin (%)';value.max='99.99';cost.value='75';value.value='25';discount.value='10';invalidate();get<HTMLFormElement>('margin-form').requestSubmit();});
get('margin-form').addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();invalidate();try{const r=calculateMargin({cost:cost.value,value:value.value,discount:discount.value,mode:mode.value});const money=(n:number)=>`${currency.value} ${n.toLocaleString('en-US',{minimumFractionDigits:2,maximumFractionDigits:2})}`;const percent=(n:number|null)=>n===null?'N/A':`${n.toFixed(2)}%`;const fields:{[key:string]:string}={price:money(r.price),discounted:money(r.discounted),'unit-cost':money(r.cost),profit:money(r.profit),percent:percent(r.margin),markup:percent(r.markup)};Object.entries(fields).forEach(([key,text])=>get(`margin-${key}`).textContent=text);get('margin-warning').textContent=r.profit<0?'This price is below your unit cost. Each sale has a gross loss.':r.discount>0?'The achieved margin includes your discount.':'';get('margin-output').hidden=false;get('margin-empty').hidden=true;summary=`KRIYANO pricing breakdown\nSelling price: ${fields.price}\nDiscount: ${r.discount}%\nAfter discount: ${fields.discounted}\nCost: ${fields['unit-cost']}\nGross profit: ${fields.profit}\nGross margin: ${fields.percent}\nMarkup: ${fields.markup}`;get('margin-status').textContent='Calculation updated.';}catch(e){get('margin-error').textContent=e instanceof Error?e.message:'Check your numbers.';}});
get('margin-copy').addEventListener('click',()=>copyText(summary,get('margin-status')));
</script>
